# ── MARK LV — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore has no trailing comments. Text after a pattern on the same
# line becomes part of the pattern, so every comment sits on its own line.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# API keys (Gemini, OpenAI, Anthropic…), plus per-plugin credentials
config/api_keys.json
config/api_keys.json.tmp
# the dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/certs/
# a LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your account
config/whatsapp_web/
# MCP servers can carry tokens
config/mcp_servers.json
# Google OAuth tokens and client secrets (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/token*.json
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db
# local transcript of what the microphone heard
memory/journal/
# scheduled assistant tasks
memory/schedule.json
memory/schedule.tmp
# face-ID embeddings of the owner
memory/faces/
# smart-home device registry (may hold local device keys)
memory/smart_home.json

# ── Downloaded models (speech, voices, faces) ─────────────────────────────────
models/

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
installer/build/
installer/dist/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
uploads/
# What the assistant learned and saw (personal, local only)
memory/knowledge.jsonl
memory/knowledge_state.json
memory/knowledge_emb.npz
memory/cctv.json
memory/cctv_events/
